DESCRIPTION >
    AI Visibility — "Pages" view. Which pages crawlers fetched, how many
    distinct crawlers touched each, and the split by category so a page read
    heavily by LLM training crawlers is distinguishable from one that only
    classic search engines index. Tenant-scoped; prunes via
    (site_id, timestamp).

    Mirrors crawler_agents.pipe on the two rules that matter: ip_mismatch rows
    are excluded from `hits` (impersonation is not the bot), and the verified /
    UA-only split is carried through rather than flattened.

    Optional `category` filter uses the `{% if defined(...) %}` block already
    proven in leads_count.pipe / browsers.pipe, with a defaulted String param
    so `tb --cloud deploy --check` has a value to inject (a required param with
    no default breaks the check — see dash_top_pages.pipe's tz note). The
    caller OMITS the param entirely for "all categories" rather than sending an
    empty string, so the block is never entered with a meaningless value.

    NOT YET DEPLOYED — founder-gated (CLAUDE.md §8); `tb --cloud deploy --check`
    has NOT been run against a workspace from here.

NODE crawler_pages_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        path,
        countIf(verification != 'ip_mismatch')                  AS hits,
        countIf(verification = 'ip_verified')                   AS hits_ip_verified,
        countIf(verification != 'ip_verified'
                AND verification != 'ip_mismatch')              AS hits_ua_only_total,
        uniqIf(bot_name, verification != 'ip_mismatch')         AS unique_bots,
        countIf(category = 'llm_crawler'
                AND verification != 'ip_mismatch')              AS hits_llm_crawler,
        countIf(category = 'ai_search'
                AND verification != 'ip_mismatch')              AS hits_ai_search,
        countIf(category = 'ai_assistant'
                AND verification != 'ip_mismatch')              AS hits_ai_assistant,
        countIf(category = 'search_engine'
                AND verification != 'ip_mismatch')              AS hits_search_engine,
        countIf(category = 'seo_tool'
                AND verification != 'ip_mismatch')              AS hits_seo_tool,
        max(timestamp)                                          AS last_seen
    FROM crawler_hits
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(from_ts, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp <= {{ DateTime(to_ts, required=True) }}
      {% if defined(category) %}
      AND category = {{ String(category, '') }}
      {% end %}
    GROUP BY path
    ORDER BY hits DESC
    LIMIT 500

TYPE endpoint
